{
  "dom_id": "step-q348060",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x{coth}^{2}⁡x+x{csch}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-{cot}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n{coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x{coth}^{2}⁡x+x{csch}^{2}⁡x}{{coth}^{4}⁡x-{csch}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x({coth}^{2}⁡x+{csch}^{2}⁡x)}{({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)({coth}^{2}⁡x+{csch}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x}{({coth}^{2}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{x}{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "field-1",
      "type": "blank",
